{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The proposed relation is 'integration', and its substantive content is the threshold formula 'net suppression = debit − credit', which requires the efficiency savings and epistemic losses to be commensurable on a common scale. But the target's own refutation clause concedes this commensurability is merely assumed, not established: the epistemic tariff (excluded rival primitives) is a diversity/opportunity-cost quantity while the efficiency savings (avoided re-derivation) is a resource-cost quantity, and nothing in the source endpoints supplies a conversion factor between them. Without that conversion, 'debit − credit' is not a well-formed arithmetic operation and the 'compound mechanism' reduces to two independent mechanisms operating in parallel — exactly the non-integration outcome the refutation clause describes. So the relation is genuinely refuted by the target's own stated condition: the endpoints as summarized do not provide the common scale the relation requires.","counterexample":[{"endpoints_provide_common_scale":false,"formula_well_defined":false,"mechanism":"independent parallel operation","net_suppression_formula":"debit − credit","refuted_by":"non-commensurability of units","relation_kind":"integration","target_concedes":"commensurability is assumed not established"}],"target_alias":"SRC_001"}]}